@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy and Terms";
}

<div class="hero" style="min-height: auto; padding: 3rem 1rem 1.5rem;">
    <div class="hero-content" style="max-width: 1000px; width: 100%;">
        <h1 class="hero-title">Privacy Policy &amp; Terms and Conditions</h1>
        <div class="verse-box text-start" style="max-width: 100%;">
            <p style="color: #ddd; margin-bottom: 0;">Tap a heading below to open or close it. Both documents are effective October 9, 2026.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    .legal-item { background: rgba(20,22,30,.95); border: 1px solid #00bfff55; border-radius: .75rem; overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; scroll-margin-top: 6rem; }
    .legal-item .accordion-button { background: transparent; color: #00bfff; box-shadow: none; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .legal-item .accordion-button:not(.collapsed) { background: #12303d; color: #00bfff; }
    .legal-item .accordion-button::after { filter: invert(60%) sepia(90%) saturate(1500%) hue-rotate(160deg); }
    .legal-item .accordion-body { color: #ddd; }
</style>

<section class="container pb-5" style="max-width: 1000px;">
<div class="accordion">
    <div class="accordion-item legal-item" id="privacy">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#privacy-body" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="privacy-body">Privacy Policy</button>
        </h2>
        <div id="privacy-body" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                <p style="color: #ddd;">England Technologies LLC collects only the information needed to schedule and perform your service, never sells it, and deletes copies of your files after the work is done. Effective October 9, 2026.</p>

    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">1. Information I Collect</h2>
        <p><strong>Booking details.</strong> When you book, the form asks for your name, email, phone number, address, city, zip code, a description of the problem, when it started, how you prefer to be contacted, and any notes you choose to add.</p>
        <p><strong>Messages.</strong> If you email, text, or call me, I keep the messages and any details you share in them.</p>
        <p><strong>Website data.</strong> Like most websites, the web server may record basic technical information, such as your IP address, browser type, the pages requested, and the date and time. I use it to keep the site secure and working.</p>
        <p><strong>Payment information.</strong> Payments are processed by Stripe. I do not see or store your full card number or wallet details. I receive a record of the payment, such as your name, email address, the amount, and the last four digits of your card. Stripe's use of your payment information is covered by its own privacy policy.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">2. How I Use It</h2>
        <p>I use your information to schedule and confirm appointments, contact you about your service, give you a plan and cost before work begins, perform the work, handle billing and business records, keep the website secure, follow the law, and resolve disputes. I do not send marketing messages unless you ask for them.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">3. Your Files and Devices During a Service</h2>
        <p>When I work on a device, I may be able to see files, photos, messages, saved passwords, and accounts. I look only at what the work needs. I copy personal files only when the service calls for it, such as a backup, a migration, or an image of a drive being recovered, and I do not share them with anyone.</p>
        <p>I do not keep your passwords. Master passwords, recovery codes, and backup codes stay with you.</p>
        <p>If I see personal information by accident while working, I keep it confidential. The one exception is illegal content, which is covered in the <a href="/legal#terms" style="color: #00bfff;">Terms and Conditions</a>.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">4. Sharing</h2>
        <p>My booking system and email run on servers that I operate myself, so your information stays under my control. I do not sell or rent your information. I share information only in these cases:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>With a service I use to deliver messages, process payments, or run a support session, such as email, text messaging, or remote-support software, and only what that service needs.</li>
            <li>When the law requires it, such as a court order or a legal request.</li>
            <li>To protect safety, prevent fraud, or defend my legal rights.</li>
            <li>If the business is sold or transferred, in which case business records may move to the new owner.</li>
        </ul>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">5. Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <p>Copies of your files that I make during a service, including backups, migration copies, and images of drives, are deleted once you confirm your files are safe. They are deleted no later than 15 days after the service, unless you ask me in writing to keep them longer, at which point I will keep the data a maximum of 60 days after the service. An automated timer will delete the data after 60 days, and there will be no extension after the 60 days are up. There is no way to undo or stop this timer.</p>
        <p>The only exception to this rule is in the event that law enforcement gets involved. In this exception, the data will be kept as long as law enforcement needs the data and will be deleted immediately after involvement with law enforcement ends.</p>
        <p>If I take ownership of equipment that was left unpaid or uncollected, as described in the <a href="/legal#terms" style="color: #00bfff;">Terms and Conditions</a>, I securely erase any data on it before it is reused, recycled, or disposed of.</p>
        <p>Booking and billing records are kept for as long as needed for business, tax, and legal purposes. Messages are kept while they are useful for supporting you.</p>
        <p>You can ask me to delete your booking information at any time. I may need to keep some records where the law requires it.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">6. Security, Cookies, and Your Choices</h2>
        <p>I use reasonable safeguards to protect your information, such as password protection, limited access to my systems, and keeping software up to date. No method of storing or sending data is completely secure, so I cannot promise absolute security. If a breach affects your information, I will notify you as the law requires.</p>
        <p>The booking system uses cookies or similar storage that it needs to work, such as keeping your session while you book. I do not use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
        <p>You can ask to see, correct, or delete the information I hold about you, or ask me to stop contacting you by email or text. Send the request through the Contact page at <a href="/contactus" style="color: #00bfff;">techsupport.englandtechnologies.net/contactus</a>.</p>
        <p>My services are for adults 18 and older. I do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18 through this website.</p>
        <p>I may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p>
    </div></div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="accordion-item legal-item" id="terms">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#terms-body" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="terms-body">Terms and Conditions</button>
        </h2>
        <div id="terms-body" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
            <div class="accordion-body">
                <p style="color: #ddd;">These terms apply to every service from England Technologies LLC and to this website. By booking an appointment or allowing work to begin, you agree to them, and you confirm that you are at least 18 years of age. Effective October 9, 2026.</p>

    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">1. Services and Scheduling</h2>
        <p>You book appointments through the website. Times that are already taken are not offered, and a booking is confirmed once you receive confirmation from the booking system. Services are performed on-site at your location or remotely, as agreed when you book.</p>
        <p>Please arrive ready: have the device, drives, passwords, and any equipment you want worked on available at the appointment. If I cannot do the work because something is missing, locked, or not as described, I may need to reschedule.</p>
        <p><strong>Safe Environment:</strong> I reserve the right to refuse service or terminate an on-site appointment immediately if the environment is unsafe, unsanitary, or hostile. If an appointment is terminated for these reasons, the $30 minimum charge and any travel fee still apply.</p>
        <p>If you need to cancel or reschedule, please give at least 24 hours of notice. There is no cancellation fee. If you repeatedly miss appointments without notice, I may decline future bookings.</p>
        <p>The session times shown for each service are estimates based on experience. Some situations may take longer and others may take less time, depending on the circumstances and the condition of your equipment.</p>
        <p>Because times are estimates and can vary, I will see as many customers as I can on the day they schedule their appointment. If I am unable to make it on that day, I will contact you to arrange another day.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">2. Pricing and Payment</h2>
        <p>Each service on the website has a flat price in US dollars. That price is what you pay for the service, whether it is done on-site or remotely, and it covers the time listed for that service. If a session needs to run past that time, the extra time is billed at $50 per hour in 15-minute increments. I will let you know before continuing past the listed time. The price shown when you book is the price for that booking, even if prices change later.</p>
        <p>Work that is not one of the listed services is billed hourly. The first hour is $65 on-site or $55 remote, then $50 per hour in 15-minute increments. Work under one hour is $1 per minute with a 30-minute minimum ($30).</p>
        <p>There is no travel fee within 25 miles of my home base, ZIP code 32259-3268, measured one way by driving distance. Beyond that, the fee is $1.50 for each mile past 25 miles. It is based on the one-way driving distance from my home base to your address, no matter what order my appointments fall in that day. Any travel fee is part of the plan and cost I give you before work begins.</p>
        <p>There is no extra charge for same-day appointments or after-hours appointments.</p>
        <p>You supply all hardware and parts. I charge for labor only. I am not responsible for the choice, compatibility, or condition of hardware you supply.</p>
        <p>Payment is due after the appointment, and I take payments through Stripe. At the end of your visit you can pay by tapping a credit or debit card, or a mobile wallet such as Apple Pay or Google Pay, on my phone. If you would rather not pay that way, or your card or phone cannot tap to pay, I will send a secure payment link to the email address on your appointment. Payment through the link is expected within 7 days of the date it is sent. After 7 days, a late fee of $4 per day applies until the balance is paid, but late fees never total more than 25% of the original amount owed. Fees for completed work are non-refundable, except where these terms say otherwise.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">3. Your Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>You are responsible for backing up your data before any work begins. Working on computers, drives, and software always carries some risk of data loss. I may offer to make a copy of your files as part of a service, but a copy made by me does not replace your own backup, and I do not guarantee that it will be complete.</p>
        <p>By booking, you confirm that you own the devices and data involved, or that the owner has given you permission to have them worked on.</p>
        <p>Please describe the problem as accurately as you can, including anything that happened beforehand, such as drops, spills, power loss, recent updates, or earlier repair attempts. Missing details can change what is possible and how long it takes.</p>
        <p>You are responsible for providing the passwords, encryption keys, and account access needed for the work. I cannot bypass a password, disk encryption, or account lock that you are unable to unlock yourself.</p>
        <p>You are responsible for having valid licenses for any software you ask me to install. I do not install pirated or unlicensed software.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">4. Data Recovery and Failing Drives</h2>
        <p>Data recovery is never guaranteed. A drive that is failing, damaged, or accidentally formatted can lose more data, or stop working entirely, at any moment. That can happen while I evaluate it, copy it, or recover files from it, and even reading a failing drive can make it worse.</p>
        <p>If a drive or device fails further, becomes unreadable, or loses data while I am evaluating or recovering it, I am not responsible and cannot be held liable for that failure, for the loss of data that could otherwise have been recovered, or for any resulting costs. By approving an evaluation or a recovery, you accept this risk.</p>
        <p>I take steps to lower the risk, such as copying a drive's readable data to an image first and working from the copy whenever possible. These steps reduce the risk but do not remove it.</p>
        <p>The 30-minute Data Recovery Evaluation checks the drive's health and what looks recoverable before you decide to continue. Its findings are an estimate, not a promise of the final result.</p>
        <p>Fees work like this:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>If you decide not to continue after the evaluation, you pay the evaluation fee only.</li>
            <li>If you approve a full recovery, you pay the full recovery price. The evaluation fee is not added on top.</li>
            <li>If I cannot recover any usable files, you pay the evaluation fee only.</li>
            <li>If I recover some but not all of your data, the full recovery price still applies, because the result depends on the condition of the drive.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Recovered files may be incomplete or damaged. When files are recovered by scanning rather than from the drive's folder structure, file names and folders are often lost. I will tell you what to expect before you approve the recovery.</p>
        <p>Recovered files are copied to a drive you provide, so please have one with enough free space ready.</p>
        <p>Some drives are not detected, click, grind, or are physically damaged. They need a specialized clean-room lab, which I do not offer. If I find this, I will stop and tell you so I do not cause more damage. Any lab you choose is a separate business, and I am not responsible for its work, prices, or results. The only thing I will provide is a suggested business or businesses to take to for the work.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">5. Other Services</h2>
        <p><strong>Malware and scam cleanup.</strong> I work to remove malicious software and unauthorized access, but I cannot guarantee that every threat is gone or that you will not be infected again. After a scam, I cannot recover money you have sent or reverse a payment. Contact your bank, card company, or the authorities as soon as you can.</p>
        <p><strong>Passwords and two-step verification.</strong> You create and keep your own master password, recovery codes, and backup codes. I do not keep copies and cannot recover them for you. Losing them can lock you out of an account permanently.</p>
        <p><strong>Secure drive sanitization.</strong> Wiping a drive is permanent and cannot be undone. Before I start, you confirm which drives to erase and that you have copies of anything you want to keep. I am not responsible for data erased from a drive you asked me to wipe. I follow accepted industry methods, but no method can guarantee a complete wipe of every drive, especially failing or damaged ones and some solid-state drives. If the data is extremely sensitive, physical destruction of the drive is safer.</p>
        <p><strong>Reinstalls, migrations, cloning, and operating system changes.</strong> These services erase or move large amounts of data. Some programs, files, or settings may not transfer, and some software does not run on every operating system, including Linux. Keep your own backup of anything that matters.</p>
        <p><strong>Hardware installation.</strong> Opening a device or installing parts can affect a manufacturer's warranty, and you accept that. I install the parts you supply but do not guarantee them. Older or worn equipment can fail on its own, and I am not responsible for failures that were already developing before I started or that are unrelated to my work.</p>
        <p><strong>Abandoned Hardware:</strong> If equipment is left unpaid or uncollected for 30 days after I send you written notice by email that it is ready, it becomes the property of England Technologies LLC. Any data on it will be securely erased before it is reused, recycled, or disposed of.</p>
        <p><strong>Networking.</strong> I change router and network settings only as needed for the service. I am not responsible for internet provider outages, equipment limits, or problems on the provider's side. I will give you any new network names and passwords I set up.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">6. Remote Sessions</h2>
        <p>Remote sessions only happen at a time we have agreed on, and only with your permission. You start the connection yourself, and you can end it at any moment. I will never contact you out of the blue and ask for remote access to your computer. If someone claiming to be me does, it is not me.</p>
        <p>During a session I access only what the work requires. Please stay near your device so you can see what is being done and answer questions. When the session ends, I remove any remote-access software I installed for it, or tell you how to remove it.</p>
        <p>A remote session needs a working internet connection on your end. I am not responsible for dropped connections, slow connections, or problems caused by your internet provider or equipment. If a problem cannot be fixed remotely, I will tell you and we can arrange an on-site visit.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">7. Privacy and Unlawful Content</h2>
        <p>Your files and information are treated as confidential. I look at your data only as far as the work requires and I do not use it for anything else. How I collect, store, and delete information is explained in the <a href="/legal#privacy" style="color: #00bfff;">England Technologies Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
        <p>I will not do work that is unlawful, such as getting into accounts or devices that are not yours, bypassing security you are not authorized to bypass, or installing pirated software. If I come across illegal content while working, especially content involving the exploitation of children, I may stop work and report it to the authorities where the law requires or allows it.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">8. Liability, Workmanship, and General Terms</h2>
        <p>I perform every service with reasonable skill and care. I cannot promise that every problem can be fixed or that your equipment will keep working afterward. If something I worked on stops working as described soon after the session, contact me through the website and I will review it.</p>
        <p>To the fullest extent the law allows, my total liability for any claim connected to a service is limited to the amount you paid for that service. I am not liable for indirect or consequential losses, such as lost income, lost profits, or downtime. Nothing in these terms limits a liability that the law does not allow to be limited.</p>
        <p>If you have a concern, please contact me first so we can try to resolve it directly. These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Florida, and any dispute that cannot be resolved directly will be handled in the courts of Florida.</p>
        <p>These terms, the <a href="/legal#privacy" style="color: #00bfff;">England Technologies Privacy Policy</a>, and the plan and price I give you before work begins make up the whole agreement between us. If any part of these terms is found unenforceable, the rest stays in effect. I may update these terms from time to time, and the version in effect when you book applies to that booking.</p>
        <p>Questions about these terms can be sent through the Contact page at <a href="/contactus" style="color: #00bfff;">techsupport.englandtechnologies.net/contactus</a>.</p>
    </div></div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</section>

@section Scripts {
<script>
    $(function () {
        // /legal#privacy or /legal#terms opens that section.
        const openFromHash = () => {
            const item = document.querySelector(location.hash === '#privacy' || location.hash === '#terms' ? location.hash : '#none');
            if (!item) return;
            bootstrap.Collapse.getOrCreateInstance(item.querySelector('.accordion-collapse'), { toggle: false }).show();
            item.scrollIntoView();
        };
        $(window).on('hashchange', openFromHash);
        openFromHash();
    });
</script>
}
